---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import whiteMosque from '../assets/photos/about-white-mosque.jpg';
import watArun from '../assets/photos/about-wat-arun.jpg';
import boracay from '../assets/photos/about-boracay.jpg';
import iraya from '../assets/photos/about-iraya.jpg';
import itbayat from '../assets/photos/about-itbayat.jpg';
import sagada from '../assets/photos/about-sagada.jpg';

// Split the available width by the native 1800×1439 and 1800×1350 aspect ratios.
const mosqueShare = 1350 / (1439 + 1350);
const firstPairShares = [mosqueShare, 1 - mosqueShare];
const photographSizes = (share: number) =>
  `(max-width: 36rem) calc(100vw - clamp(2.5rem, 10vw, 7rem)), calc((min(100vw, 78rem) - clamp(2.5rem, 10vw, 7rem) - clamp(1rem, 2.6vw, 2.5rem)) * ${share})`;
const photographWidths = [320, 360, 480, 560, 640, 720, 960, 1120, 1280, 1440, 1680];

const photographs = [
  {
    src: whiteMosque,
    alt: 'A white mosque with turquoise doors and arched windows beside the sea, framed by palms.',
    place: 'Tawi-Tawi',
    year: 2016,
  },
  {
    src: watArun,
    alt: 'Gold-lit temple spires and a roof with rain streaking across the night sky.',
    place: 'Bangkok',
    year: 2018,
    widths: [...photographWidths, 1720],
  },
  {
    src: boracay,
    alt: 'Two paddleboarders silhouetted against the setting sun, with sailboats on the horizon.',
    place: 'Boracay',
    year: 2017,
  },
  {
    src: iraya,
    alt: 'Mount Iraya across blue water, seen from a grassy headland.',
    place: 'Basco',
    year: 2016,
  },
  {
    src: itbayat,
    alt: 'People carrying bags on a red-roofed faluwa beside a rocky landing.',
    place: 'Itbayat',
    year: 2015,
  },
  {
    src: sagada,
    alt: 'A wooden café with a green awning among pines, with mountains in the distance.',
    place: 'Sagada',
    year: 2015,
  },
];
const photoPairs = [photographs.slice(0, 2), photographs.slice(2, 4), photographs.slice(4, 6)];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Archieval Mariano"
  description="Archieval Mariano is a digital strategy and audience growth professional based in the Philippines, working across content, analytics, e-commerce, and digital operations."
>
  <article class="wrap about">
    <header class="about-cover">
      <h1>Archieval Mariano</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="storyteller">
      <h2 id="storyteller">The bored storyteller</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>I actually remember the first time I used that name. The storyteller part, at least.</p>
        <p>I was in El Nido with my college friends, and we were talking to some tourists from Québec. The conversation eventually turned to what we all did for a living. At the time, I wasn't really getting paid to write, and "writer" just felt flat.</p>
        <p class="about-aside">Also, we wanted to impress some particularly pretty people.</p>
        <blockquote class="about-dialogue">
          <p>"Are you an artist, too?" one of them asked, referring to what my friend had said.</p>
          <p>"No, not at all. I'm a storyteller."</p>
        </blockquote>
        <p>Polite nods. I think a lot was lost in translation. What was the French equivalent of what I was trying to convey, anyway? My friends exchanged knowing smiles, and the conversation eventually drifted to teaching one another useful swear words.</p>
        <p>The moniker stuck, so I continued using it.</p>
        <p>"Bored" came later. Why not?</p>
        <p>Perhaps there's a better word for a storyteller who's always looking for interesting stories to make, share, or laugh about over beer. Or, these days, my drink of choice: non-alcoholic anything.</p>
        <p>But I kept <em>bored</em> because, in a strange way, it describes an aspiration. You can't really be bored when there's still so much to do, so much to discover, and so many stories left to write. Boredom, I suppose, is what happens when you've finally run out of them.</p>
        <p class="about-aside">I haven't. Not even close.</p>
        <p class="about-aside">Or I'm not making sense. You tell me.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="expression">
      <h2 id="expression">Part expression, part puzzle</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>I've always been drawn to the way a word can change meaning through context, placement, or tone. I still enjoy taking a familiar fact, trope, or saying and turning it on its head. For me, writing has always been part expression and part puzzle.</p>
        <p>That instinct eventually led me beyond copy. Data is another way of finding a narrative. Strategy is deciding which patterns matter and what to do with them. Operations turn that conclusion into something people can repeat.</p>
        <p>They're different materials, but I approach them with the same desire to make something complicated clearer.</p>
        <p>The path has taken me through editorial, branded content, e-commerce, analytics, audience development, digital strategy, and the systems that connect them. I still find myself moving between these disciplines, often borrowing something from one to solve a problem in another.</p>
        <aside class="about-experience" aria-labelledby="experience">
          <h3 id="experience">Selected experience</h3>
          <p>GMA New Media Inc. · SM Investments Corporation · Summit Media · Independent consulting</p>
          <p><em>More than a decade across digital work.</em></p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="away">
      <h2 id="away">Away from the dashboards</h2>
      <div class="about-prose">
        <p>From the ugly chicken-scratch handwriting of my younger years to the loud (and absolutely satisfying) clacking of my keyboard nowadays, it seems I've been writing my whole life.</p>
        <p>After a couple of drinks, I might even admit that I'm good at it. Among other things.</p>
        <p>Photography came a little later. I remember getting through our photojournalism class with just my phone, using captions as a crutch to coast to a good grade.</p>
        <p>Then, in my twenties, I bought my first "serious" Micro Four Thirds camera. I fell in love with a Panasonic pancake lens, swore off zoom lenses, and eventually decided that cameras were tedious. Editing, even more so.</p>
        <p>So I swore off cameras in favor of phones. Then I circled back to serious cameras. Or two. Or three.</p>
        <p>These days, I've settled on a Fujifilm X100VI. I'm not quite brave enough to shoot JPEG only, but I do like not having to adjust much afterward.</p>
        <p>I like liminal photography. Or perhaps I just really dislike having people in my frame.</p>
        <p>I write poetry, although no amount of alcohol in the world will make me call myself a poet. I like technology, too, and I might have an unhealthy obsession with e-ink.</p>
        <p>I also travel. In my twenties, I built trips around hostels and long journeys over land, saving on comfort so I could spend more on experience. I still travel, but I no longer treat discomfort as proof that a trip mattered. I move more slowly now, chase fewer attractions, and leave more room to notice what's actually there.</p>
        <p>My friends and family will vouch for my skills as a conversationalist. Or a know-it-all, depending on whom you ask.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-photographs" aria-labelledby="photographs">
      <h2 id="photographs">Selected photographs</h2>
      <div class="about-photos" oncontextmenu="return false">
        {photoPairs.map((pair, row) => (
          <div
            class="about-photos__pair"
            style={row === 0 ? { '--left-share': `${firstPairShares[0]}fr`, '--right-share': `${firstPairShares[1]}fr` } : undefined}
          >
            {pair.map((photo, column) => (
              <figure>
                <Image
                  src={photo.src}
                  alt={photo.alt}
                  width={1120}
                  widths={photo.widths ?? photographWidths}
                  sizes={photographSizes(row === 0 ? firstPairShares[column] : 0.5)}
                  format="webp"
                  quality={89}
                  loading="lazy"
                  draggable="false"
                />
                <figcaption>{photo.place}, <span>{photo.year}</span></figcaption>
              </figure>
            ))}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav class="about-links" aria-label="Continue exploring">
      <a href="/work/">Work</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/desk/">Desk</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
      <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about-cover {
    padding-block: clamp(3.25rem, 7vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 3.25rem);
  }

  .about-cover h1 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(4.2rem, 9vw, 8.5rem);
    font-weight: 780;
    letter-spacing: -.035em;
    line-height: .9;
  }

  .about-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 16rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md) clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
    align-items: start;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .about-section:first-of-type {
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.75rem);
  }

  .about-section h2,
  .about-photographs h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 740;
    letter-spacing: -.035em;
  }

  .about-prose {
    max-width: 62ch;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.16rem, 1.45vw, 1.36rem);
    line-height: 1.56;
  }

  .about-prose p { margin: 0; }
  .about-prose > p + p { margin-top: .9em; }
  .about-prose > .about-aside { margin-block: 1.1em; }

  .about-dialogue {
    margin: 1.3em 0;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--coral);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .about-dialogue p + p { margin-top: .55em; }

  .about-experience {
    margin: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.75rem) 0 0;
    padding: clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem) clamp(1rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    background-color: var(--yellow);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .about-experience h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 730;
    letter-spacing: .02em;
  }

  .about-experience p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .about-photographs {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-block: var(--space-lg) var(--space-xl);
  }

  .about-photographs h2 { position: relative; }

  .about-photographs h2::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-block-start: .16em;
    inset-inline-start: -.45em;
    width: 2px;
    height: .72em;
    background: var(--coral);
  }

  .about-photos {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about-photos__pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, var(--left-share, 1fr)) minmax(0, var(--right-share, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1rem, 2.6vw, 2.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-photos__pair:first-child { align-items: stretch; }

  .about-photos__pair:first-child figure {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .about-photos figure { min-width: 0; margin: 0; }
  .about-photos img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

  .about-photos figcaption {
    margin-top: .65rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 550;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .about-photos figcaption span {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .about-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: .35rem .85rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 680;
  }

  .about-links a {
    display: inline-block;
    padding-block: .3rem;
  }

  .about-links a:hover,
  .about-links a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--accent-ink);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  .about-links span { color: var(--ink-faint); }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .about-section { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-sm); }
  }

  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .about-cover h1 { font-size: min(4.2rem, 18vw); }
    .about-photos,
    .about-photos__pair { gap: var(--space-lg); }
    .about-photos__pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
